# <%= className %> GraphQL service

Location: `apps/<%= fileName %>`. NestJS, code-first GraphQL via `@nestjs/graphql` + Apollo.

## Layout

- `src/app.module.ts` — `GraphQLModule.forRoot` with `ApolloDriver`, `autoSchemaFile: src/schema.gql` (generated at runtime, gitignored), playground on.
- `src/app.resolver.ts` — resolvers; one `@Query()` / `@Mutation()` method per GraphQL field.
- `src/app.service.ts` — business logic the resolvers call.
- `src/main.ts` — plain HTTP bootstrap (`PORT` env, default 3000). GraphQL is served at `/graphql`.

## Adding a query or mutation

1. Define input/output types as classes decorated `@ObjectType()` / `@InputType()`
   with `@Field()` on each property (code-first — no `.graphql` files).
2. Add a method to a `@Resolver()` class decorated `@Query(() => T)` or
   `@Mutation(() => T)`. The schema regenerates on next start.
3. Keep resolver methods thin; put logic in a service.

## Running

```bash
nx serve <%= fileName %>      # nest start --watch, playground at http://localhost:3000/graphql
nx build <%= fileName %>
nx test <%= fileName %>
```

Deps are not installed by the generator — run `npm install` in `apps/<%= fileName %>` first.
